      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63884e706df0d253eb674deb|full_name} Is selling group permissions even a thing within the creator economy? I always assumed that when people, for example, bought priority queue at a club (a practice I also frown upon), that would have to be done elsewhere and someone would have to manually add the position or write an external script that does it.",
